      "text": "agent_b detailed findings. 61 test, exactly 16 deaths (positive class for F1 = death/1). Ticket-group transfer is ~100% reliable when a female shares a ticket with a female train-mate (use that outcome); single-male-mate-died is NOT reliable (only 35% of those females die). My SOLID labels: DIE = {77171, 98361, 20080, 93404, 15198, 90011} (all have female groupmate(s) who died). SURV = {21692, 76818, 32156, 58368, 84801, 10227, 83878, 75766, 22315, 69323, 49164, 60326, 50830, 92967} (female groupmate alive or male groupmate alive). Exact feature-match also supports: 98291=DIE, 17109/99582/99888/77552/60316=SURV. 96648 & 17550 share ticket 19950 (P1 large family, male mate died) - possibly both DIE. I'll now probe candidates."
